AI attack score details:
```
function chooseAiAttack() {
 const me='enemy', foe='player';
 const attackers=G.monsters(me).filter(c=>!c.destroying && !attackReasonInternal(c));
 let best=null;
 for (const a of attackers) {
   const v=validTargets(a);
   const atkA=G.effAtk(a);
   if (v.direct && (!v.monsters.length || hasMod(a,'direct'))) {
      const score=atkA + (G.player(foe).lp<=atkA?10000:0);
      if(!best||score>best.score) best={attacker:a,target:null,score};
   }
   for(const t of v.monsters){
     if(t.destroying) continue;
     const atkD=G.effAtk(t);
     let score;
     if(atkA>atkD){
       const dmg=atkA-atkD;
       score=800+dmg*1.4+(t.defId==='golem'?100:0);
       if(G.player(foe).lp<=dmg) score+=10000;
       if(hasMod(t,'battleShield')) score-=350;
     } else if(atkA===atkD){
       score=250 + G.effAtk(t)*0.2;
       if(hasMod(t,'battleShield')) score-=200;
     } else {
       score=-900;
     }
     if(score>0 && (!best||score>best.score)) best={attacker:a,target:t,score};
   }
 }
 return best;
}
```
If direct and monsters both, direct score atk; beating a monster score often higher. Good. If atkA<atkD for all and no direct, no attack.
Taunt with battleShield and low ATK may force skip; fine.
If enemy monsters exist but direct mod, v.direct true; if v.monsters includes only taunt, direct bypasses taunt. AI may choose direct. Fine.
