Now part 3: AI. Need scheduleAi/runAi and helper functions using renderAll, executeAct, performAttack, placeCard. Define AI functions.

Details:
```
function scheduleAi() {
 const token=++S.aiRun;
 setTimeout(()=>runAi(token), 700);
}
```
But restart increments aiRun; fine.

`aiAlive(token)` checks.

`runAi`:
```
async function runAi(token) {
 if (!aiAlive(token)) return;
 S.busy=true; renderAll();
 await waitModal(token);
 await sleep(500);
 if (!aiAlive(token)) return;
 await aiTakeTurn(token);
 if (!aiAlive(token)) return;
 await sleep(350);
 if (!aiAlive(token)) return;
 await finishTurn();
}
```
Note `finishTurn` uses S.active; must still be enemy. `aiAlive` includes active check.

`waitModal(token)` while modalOpen && aiAlive(token).

`aiTakeTurn`:
- Summon.
- Set relic.
- Acts.
- Extra summon.
- Attacks.

Need `aiPlace(card)` using placeCard:
```
function aiSummon() {
 const cards=S.players[ENEMY].hand.filter(c=>defOf(c).kind==='monster');
 if(!cards.length || emptyBig(ENEMY)<0 || p.summonUsed>=1+p.extraSummons) return false;
 const best=...;
 placeCard(best); return true;
}
```
`placeCard` calls renderAll and sfx; AI busy stays. Good.

AI set:
```
function aiSet() { p.setUsed<1; hand relics; ... placeCard }
```

`chooseAiAct`:
Build candidates. Consider `S.players[ENEMY].ward>0` → sort ascending.
Need avoid using act that would kill self? canAct guards. Archive at LP 600 allowed (lp>500) leaves 100; AI might; score lower if lp<1200. Add guards in scores.

Act score function with all defIds. Let's write a comprehensive switch.

```
function aiActScore(card) {
 const id=card.defId; const p=S.players[ENEMY], foe=S.players[PLAYER];
 const fm=monsters(PLAYER), mm=monsters(ENEMY);
 const strongestFoe=highestAtk(PLAYER), strongestMine=highestAtk(ENEMY);
 switch(id) {
  case 'flarewolf': return 55;
  case 'golem': return fm.length?60:20;
  case 'twinblade': return fm.length && canAttackNow(card)?85:10;
  case 'witch': return p.hand.length<=4 && p.lp>600?55:15;
  case 'varga': { if(!strongestFoe) return 0; const value=effAtk(strongestFoe); return p.lp>900? (value>=1600?110:75) : 0; }
  case 'seraph': return p.lp<2200?95:0;
  case 'hayate': { const bigHand=S.players[ENEMY].hand.some(c=>defOf(c).kind==='monster' && defOf(c).atk>=1700); return bigHand && emptyBig(ENEMY)>=0?30:0; } // emptyBig before bounce is -? if field full, after bounce empty
  case 'leviathan': return relics(PLAYER).length && p.lp>900?55:0;
  case 'magnet': return strongestFoe && effAtk(strongestFoe)>=1400?75:15;
  case 'chrono': return p.lp>900?50:0;
  case 'sprout': return emptyBig(ENEMY)>=0 && mm.length<4?50:0;
  case 'blade': return mm.length?70:0;
  case 'shield': return mm.length && fm.length?55:20;
  case 'bolt': return 85;
  case 'fountain': return p.lp<2200?100:0;
  case 'archive': return p.lp>1200 && p.hand.length<=4?65:0;
  case 'revival': return graveMonsters(ENEMY).length && emptyBig(ENEMY)>=0 && p.lp>800?85:0;
  case 'ring': return actedMonsters(ENEMY).some(c=>effAtk(c)>=1500)?65:0;
  case 'vortex': { const e=relics(PLAYER).length, m=relics(ENEMY).length; return e>=2 && e>m?70:0; }
  case 'crystal': return 55;
  case 'altar': return 35;
  case 'bounce': return strongestFoe && effAtk(strongestFoe)> (strongestMine?effAtk(strongestMine):0)?85:40;
 }
 return 0;
}
```
Hayate: if field emptyBig>=0 already, after bounce extra; if field full, bounce creates space. Condition should be hand monster and (emptyBig>=0 || full field?) Actually Hayate itself occupies a big zone; bouncing frees it. So always after bounce an empty zone exists. Check hand has monster. `emptyBig` after bounce not needed. Score 30 if hand monster >=1700. But AI's summon loop second pass will summon. Good.

Note `canAttackNow(card)` checks owner active; AI active yes. Twinblade if summoned this turn can't attack; then its act direct is wasted; score 0 if summoning sick. Use `card.summonedSerial===S.turnSerial` check.

`chooseAiAct` filters `canActNow(card)` null; then score > 0. If ward>0 choose lowest score (burn shield). But if score 0 acts? canAct yes; use min including 10. Let's collect all and if ward choose min by score (even 0). Else max > 0.

Wait: canActNow returns string/ null. It doesn't check owner active; use `if (canActNow(card)) continue;`.
AI can act with card whose owner is enemy. Fine.

AI set choice:
```
function aiRelicChoice() {
 const hand=...; score relic for set (not act):
 fountain if lp<2200 100; revival if grave & empty 90; archive if hand<=4 80; blade if monsters 75; shield if enemy strongest 65; bolt 60; crystal 55; ring if acted 50; bounce if enemy strong 45; altar 30; vortex 40; leviathan? monster no.
}
```
The relic's act will be available next turn; setting doesn't act this turn. AI acts after setting! If it sets a relic then in act loop it can immediately use its act because `placeCard` sets acted=false. So AI can set and activate same turn. Nice. Then set choice should consider immediate act; use same score. But AI set limit 1 and act loop includes it. Choose best relic by aiActScore for relic cards in hand; if score >0 place. That's good. However if it sets crystal, then immediately ward; okay. If it sets archive, draw. Fine. Use highest score among hand relics (with score tie by id). If all score 0 (e.g., no target), still maybe set something for future? Set fountain at full (score 0) could be useful later. But only 1 set/turn; setting for future is good. Choose highest even if 0. Fine.

Order: summon → set → acts. Setting a relic then immediately acting uses it; good.

AI attack:
Need ensure validTargets uses `attacker.owner` (enemy) and `S.active` enemy. Good.
Use `canAttackNow` null.
Score and pick.

Also AI should use Twinblade direct mod: after act, `hasMod(attacker,'direct')`, validTargets direct true. Good.
AI should use Blade buff then attack; buff applies to highestAtk, possibly the attacker. Good.

Extra summon after acts: If Hayate used, summonUsed maybe 1, extra=1 → can summon. If AI set no big? fine.
```
if (p.summonUsed < 1+p.extraSummons) aiSummon();
```

AI loop cap; check token.

`waitModal` if modal open. Also if game over, break.

Attack loop picks plans; if plan target null direct. `performAttack` ai sets busy stays true.

AI may attack with a monster that was refreshed by Ring etc. Good.

AI should not act with a card then have it destroyed mid-loop; loop recomputes candidates each time.

`aiAlive` requires S.active===ENEMY. After checkGameOver S.over true; break.

Potential modal pause during executeAct: if player opens rules during AI's sleep, next wait catches; fine.

Let's append.

